blew — vendored, modified copy
==============================

This directory contains a vendored copy of the Rust half of `blew`, a
cross-platform async Bluetooth Low Energy library (Apple, Linux, Android).

Upstream project : https://github.com/mcginty/blew
Upstream version : 0.3.0 (crates.io; git tag `blew-v0.3.0`,
                   commit dde4bdaa09b3ef60bb595dd1be360a54c17615d4, crates/blew)
Original author  : Jake McGinty <me@jakebot.org>
License          : GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later
                   (AGPL-3.0-or-later) — see the `LICENSE` file in this
                   directory for the full license text.

This modified copy remains licensed under AGPL-3.0-or-later, the same license
as the upstream project.

The Android Kotlin half of blew was vendored separately, in July 2026, into
modules/iroh-location/android/src/main/java/org/jakebot/blew/ (notice in
modules/iroh-location/android/third_party/blew/). It is not duplicated here,
and upstream's `android/`, `examples/` and `tests/` directories are omitted.


Modifications by the streetCryptid project
------------------------------------------

In accordance with section 5 of the GNU AGPL, the changes made to the upstream
0.3.0 source after it was vendored into this repository are dated and
described below.

2026-10-31 — Apple flow control (CoreBluetooth backend):

  * Cargo.toml
      - Added this vendoring header, `publish = false`, and removed the
        `include` list. Added `objc2-core-foundation` (Apple targets) for the
        L2CAP reactor's run-loop source.

  * build.rs
      - `android_dir` now points at the module's vendored Kotlin sources.

  * src/platform/apple/peripheral.rs
      - `notify_characteristic` no longer drops a notification when
        CoreBluetooth's transmit queue is full. Upstream ignored the return
        value of `updateValue:forCharacteristic:onSubscribedCentrals:`; it now
        waits for `peripheralManagerIsReadyToUpdateSubscribers:` (new delegate
        method) and sends the value again, for at most 2 s.

  * src/platform/apple/central.rs
      - A write without response is sent only when `canSendWriteWithoutResponse`
        is true; otherwise it waits for
        `peripheralIsReadyToSendWriteWithoutResponse:` (new delegate method),
        for at most 2 s. Upstream wrote unconditionally, which CoreBluetooth may
        drop silently.

  * src/platform/apple/l2cap.rs
      - The reactor thread no longer polls its run loop every 50 ms. Commands
        signal a `CFRunLoopSource` attached to the run loop, which also stops
        an idle reactor from spinning when no stream is scheduled.
      - Writes check `hasSpaceAvailable` before `write:maxLength:`, keep bytes
        the stream cannot take yet in a per-channel queue, and no longer close
        the channel when a write returns 0. The Rust-side bridge stops reading
        from the app while 64 KiB are queued (back-pressure).
